  ],
  "details": "<p>The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Tangier. There are discrepant readings of the origins of the ancient name\u00a0<em>Tingis</em>. Some suggest a Berber origin, while some Greek sources claimed that the name derived from that of a daughter of the Titan Atlas.</p>",
  "review_state": "published",
  "type": "FeatureCollection",
  "description": "Tingi (modern Tangier) began as a Carthaginian colony of the early fifth century BCE. A commercial center, Tingi came under the Roman sphere in the first century BCE, initially as a free city but later as the site of a colony (Colonia Julia) under Claudius and the capital of Mauritania Tingitana.",
